# Re-run mic/AEC reconciliation whenever ALSA sound cards appear or
# disappear. The reconciler is cheap and idempotent: it only flips
# service/env state when the current mic config is one JTS owns (a
# registry card name, udp:PORT, or a configured candidate). Custom
# JASPER_MIC_DEVICE values are left alone.
#
# Keyed to sound control nodes, not a hard-coded XVF USB id. Supported mic
# identity lives in the mic profile registry and reaches the reconciler
# through `jasper-xvf-profile --env` (ADR-0235); JASPER_MIC_DEVICE_CANDIDATES
# only overrides that list. The policy stays in the reconciler.

ACTION=="add|remove", SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="controlC*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="jasper-aec-reconcile.service"
